Neuter cmInstrumentation::GetDynamicSystemInformation on illumos.

Every real (non-try-compile) `cmake` configure calls this method, which on
Solaris has cmsys SystemInformation shell out (psrinfo/kstat) via popen ->
posix_spawn. This illumos kernel (68259130da) lacks the SYS_spawn fast path and
its libc does not fall back to fork/exec, so the spawn syscall returns ENOSYS
and the process takes SIGSYS ("Bad System Call", core dump). The dynamic
sysinfo is pure telemetry (host memory / CPU load in a JSON blob) and never
affects the build, so make the probe a no-op.
--- a/Source/cmInstrumentation.cxx
+++ b/Source/cmInstrumentation.cxx
@@ -460,6 +460,7 @@
 void cmInstrumentation::GetDynamicSystemInformation(double& memory,
                                                     double& load)
 {
+  memory = 0; load = 0; return;
   cmsys::SystemInformation& info = this->GetSystemInformation();
   if (!this->ranSystemChecks) {
     info.RunCPUCheck();
